 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nbrain_attrs doesn't add PEP 526 instance variable annotations, causing `no-member` errors\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nIn some contexts, Pylint issues a false positive with an attrs class with only a type annotation (see [PEP 526](https://peps.python.org/pep-0526/#class-and-instance-variable-annotations). If we add the attribute via the astroid brain_attrs then this fixes the issue. (I'm not sure if this is a duplicate of #724 ). This is supported at runtime with the newer `attrs` decorators.\r\n\r\n```py\r\n# pylint: disable=missing-docstring,too-few-public-methods,unnecessary-lambda-assignment\r\nimport attrs  # pylint: disable=import-error\r\n\r\n@attrs.define\r\nclass AttrsCls:\r\n    x: int\r\n\r\nac = AttrsCls(1)\r\nac.x += 1\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### Current behavior\r\n\r\n```\r\nregression_xxxx_attrs_no_member.py:13: [E1101(no-member), ] Instance of 'AttrsCls' has no 'x' member\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n_No error_\n</issue>\n",
